{
  "correction_rules": [
    "Strong upward-trend underestimation: when the last 5–10 days show a clear rally (positive slope/series of higher closes), add a positive level shift to the whole path. In these examples the model is ~+0.5 to +1 EUR low at days 1–3, widening to ~+8 to +13 EUR low by days 15–30.",
    "Horizon-dependent bias: apply an increasing uplift with forecast horizon (e.g., small +0–1 EUR near-term, ramping linearly to a large uplift by day 30) rather than a constant offset; errors grow with time, indicating trend/acceleration is missing.",
    "Lag in capturing breakouts: after a regime change (price breaks above prior 30d range), the model mean-reverts back toward ~69–72 while reality continues trending up into the high-70s/low-80s. Reduce mean-reversion strength when price is making new 20–30d highs.",
    "Volatility/convexity underpricing: the model’s forecast path is too smooth and capped; true outcomes show sustained higher levels after jumps. Increase responsiveness to momentum (e.g., amplify recent returns) and allow higher ceilings in bullish regimes.",
    "Post-spike behavior mis-specified: model expects pullbacks after initial rise, but realized series consolidates at higher levels. Replace 'pullback after spike' with 'plateau at new level' when the spike is accompanied by multi-day follow-through."
  ]
}
